## Objective
- Autonomously test authorized target `account.ui.com` for valid, reproducible client-side and server-side vulnerabilities, following `skills/AGENT.md` exactly and reporting results under `result/`.

## Important Details
- Authorization source: `data/targets.txt`; scope is `account.ui.com` only plus same-origin components required to exercise it.
- Do not expand to sibling subdomains, third-party services, CDNs, or partner systems. Existing `result/scope.md` documents a backend exception for `sso.ui.com`, `account.svc.ui.com`, `geo.svc.ui.com`, `fabric.svc.ui.com`, and `ecomm.svc.ui.com` only as required by the `account.ui.com` SPA.
- Required workflow: discover unique UI routes, test one route at a time, wait 5–10 seconds for JS load, test client-side then server-side, document each route, maintain progress report.
- User requested two test accounts; account creation has been blocked by reCAPTCHA Enterprise. Do not bypass CAPTCHA.
- Provided creds in `creds/test-account.txt` are unrelated to this target and were not used.
- Current target state: `decision=preserved`, `target_hash=ff311b9fcf5fa16d5c8d15bb89a4bb1f1d84e7a625dc0acb53dec02e1accd998`.
- Bundle under test: `result/client-side/account.ui.com/_global/javascript/index-D5t7M7xo.js`, sha256 `ce9950c975a42cac66f5c2ea759d655e96c441d34df6a6b8190b09d60ea1c468`.
- Static analysis so far found no app-level user-controlled `innerHTML` sink; CSP blocks `eval`; postMessage listeners validate origin; no open redirect found.
- Key redirect primitives: `MC` allows only `http(s)` hosts ending in `ui.com`, `ubnt.com`, `uisp.com`; `Wpe` allowlists local paths and rejects `//`/backslashes; `DQ`/`CQ` validate redirects.
- Suspicious special case `S7e`: for `pathname === "/"` with hash `#reset-password/password-reset-uuid` or `#verify/verification-code`, returns `/${hash.slice(1)}` without `Wpe`, but resulting path remains same-origin.
- Chrome DevTools MCP is available; Chrome is running headless on `127.0.0.1:9222`, selected page `about:blank`.
- `result/confirmed-vuln.txt` currently contains no confirmed vulnerabilities.

## Work State
### Completed
- Read `skills/AGENT.md`, `skills/client-side-skill.md`, and `skills/server-side-skill.md`.
- Completed preflight: repo layout, tools, git status, target state, scope, existing result files.
- Confirmed live site returns HTTP 200 and current bundle hash matches prior analysis.
- Reviewed existing `result/scope.md`, `result/route-progress.md`, `result/route-reports.md`, `result/findings/observations.md`, and `result/server-side/account.ui.com/api-inventory.md`.
- Extracted and reviewed route literals, API paths, `postMessage` listeners, `dangerouslySetInnerHTML`/`innerHTML` sinks, and redirect helpers from the bundle.
- Tested URL parser edge cases for the `MC` allowlist; no bypass to arbitrary external hosts found.
- Searched public disclosure reports for prior Ubiquiti/account.ui.com issues; no directly applicable confirmed finding.
- Recorded session start in `result/logs/session.md` at `2026-10-30T05:04:06Z`.

### Active
- Continuing in-scope unauthenticated/manual route testing and static review for reportable XSS, CSTI, IDOR/BAC, or open redirect.
- Investigating residual query-param and hash-based redirect behaviors, especially `S7e`, `b7e`, `x7e`, `redirect`, and `innerRedirect`.
- Evaluating whether any route or API behavior is a real vulnerability rather than informational/account-enumeration behavior.

### Blocked
- Cannot create the requested test accounts because registration is protected by reCAPTCHA Enterprise.
- Many authenticated routes and server-side endpoints cannot be fully exercised without valid accounts.
- Scope ambiguity for `sso.ui.com` and other UI backends: prior work used them as documented backend exception, but strict `AGENT.md` rules prohibit unapproved expansion.

## Next Move
1. Continue one-by-one unauthenticated route testing with Chrome DevTools MCP, starting with `/register`, `/login`, `/verify`, `/reset-password`, and `/switch`, capturing network traffic and checking DOM/runtime sinks with harmless markers.
2. Update `result/route-progress.md`, `result/route-reports.md`, and `result/findings/observations.md` with exact route status and evidence; only add to `result/confirmed-vuln.txt` if a reproducible vulnerability is proven.

## Relevant Files
- `skills/AGENT.md`: master workflow and non-negotiable authorization/safety rules.
- `skills/client-side-skill.md`: client-side testing methodology.
- `skills/server-side-skill.md`: server-side/API testing methodology.
- `data/targets.txt`: authorized target and user instructions.
- `creds/README.md` and `creds/test-account.txt`: available credentials; currently unrelated to target.
- `result/scope.md`: scope/authorization assumptions and backend exception.
- `result/route-progress.md`: route discovery/test progress tracker.
- `result/route-reports.md`: existing per-route findings and verdicts.
- `result/findings/observations.md`: informational findings such as user-existence oracle and public client keys.
- `result/server-side/account.ui.com/api-inventory.md`: discovered API endpoint inventory.
- `result/client-side/account.ui.com/_global/javascript/index-D5t7M7xo.js`: primary SPA bundle under review.
- `result/logs/target-state.txt`: current run/hash/decision state.
- `result/logs/session.md`: session start record.
- `result/confirmed-vuln.txt`: confirmed vulnerability ledger; currently empty.
